  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal obligated $2.2B in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date, across 190 awards with an average award size of $11.6M. Obligations are down 37.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.2B, followed by the General Services Administration at $762M and the Department of Homeland Security at $148M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for CACI Federal work at $877M, with Engineering Services next at $535M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M. Historical obligations show growth through FY25, with totals listed for FY21 through FY26. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date contract obligations. The dataset includes agency and market breakdowns but does not provide award-value detail for specific expiring contracts in the summary tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are CACI Federal obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.2B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is the second-largest buyer with $762M, and the Department of Homeland Security is third with $148M. Smaller obligations include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $108M and the Department of the Interior at $24.9M, while the Department of Health and Human Services shows $0."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets drive CACI Federal obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the top market at $877M, followed by Engineering Services at $535M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is $175M, and Other Computer Related Services is $114M. The top markets together account for the bulk of FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CACI Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CACI Federal made $2.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal recorded 190 awards for that period with an average award size of $11.6M, and obligations are down 37.1% year over year. Historical annual obligations listed are $1.3B for FY21, $1.7B for FY22, $2.3B for FY23, $2.8B for FY24, and $3.5B for FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CACI Federal?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, General Services Administration, and Department of Homeland Security are the primary buyers of CACI Federal work. The Department of Defense obligated $1.2B, the General Services Administration obligated $762M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $148M in FY2026 to date. Other listed buyers include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $108M and the Department of the Interior at $24.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
      "a": "CACI Federal sells primarily Computer Systems Design Services, Engineering Services, and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $877M, Engineering Services accounts for $535M, and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services accounts for $194M in FY2026 to date. The data also shows R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $175M and Other Computer Related Services at $114M."
    },
